==Portuguese==

===Etymology===
{{lit|river of January}}. The city was named after the [[Guanabara|Guanabara Bay]] (the word {{m|pt|rio}}, which in modern Portuguese means “river”, could also mean other [[water body|water bodies]] such as bays in the 16th century) and the date it was discovered by Portuguese founders: January 1, 1502.

